SUMMARY:Yilin Wu (Luxembourg) : Graded Higgs categories
DESCRIPTION:Abstract: Let A be a differential bigraded k-algebra and let e be an idempotent of A. Under suitable assumptions on the pair (A\,e)\, we define the graded Higgs category H and the graded relative cluster category C. We show that H carries a Frobenius extriangulated structure\, and that its stable category admits a silting object. Examples arise from Keller-Scherotzke's work on graded singular Nakajim\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16841/
LOCATION:IHP\, 11 rue Pierre et Marie Curie\, Paris 5e
URL:https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16841/
