DESCRIPTION:The m-th jet scheme of an algebraic variety $X\\subset \\mathbf{A}^n$\, roughly speaking\, parametrizes germs of curves in the ambient space $\\mathbf{A}^n$ having contact of order at least m+1 with X. As m varies\, jet schemes contain a large amount of information about the singularities of $X$\, but this information is often difficult to analyze directly\, as it appears in a highly redundant and unstruc\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/15134/
